{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@preconcurrency","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"map","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transformed","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transform","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@escaping","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" (","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncSequence\/Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci12_ConcurrencyE3mapyAA24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceVyxqd__Gqd__7ElementQzYaKclF11TransformedL_qd__mfp","text":"Transformed","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/AsyncThrowingMapSequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceV","text":"AsyncThrowingMapSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transformed","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci12_ConcurrencyE3mapyAA24AsyncThrowingMapSequenceVyxqd__Gqd__7ElementQzYaKclF11TransformedL_qd__mfp"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A mapping closure. "},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" accepts an element"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of this sequence as its parameter and returns a transformed value of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same or of a different type. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transform"},{"type":"text","text":" can also throw an error, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends the transformed sequence."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"transform"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An asynchronous sequence that contains, in order, the elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produced by the "},{"code":"transform","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" closure."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method to transform every element received from a base"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asynchronous sequence. Typically, you use this to transform from one type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of element to another."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In this example, an asynchronous sequence called ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"text":" produces ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"5"},{"type":"text","text":". The closure provided to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes each "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and looks up a corresponding "},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"romanNumeralDict","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" dictionary. This means the outer "},{"code":"for await in","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" loop"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterates over "},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instances instead of the underlying "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that "},{"code":"Counter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" produces. Also, the dictionary doesn’t provide a key for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"4","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the closure throws an error for any key it can’t look up, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receiving this value from "},{"code":"Counter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ends the modified sequence with an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"error."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let romanNumeralDict: [Int: String] =","    [1: \"I\", 2: \"II\", 3: \"III\", 5: \"V\"]","","do {","    let stream = Counter(howHigh: 5)","        .map { (value) throws -> String in","            guard let roman = romanNumeralDict[value] else {","                throw MyError()","            }","            return roman","        }","    for try await numeral in stream {","        print(numeral, terminator: \" \")","    }","} catch {","    print(\"Error: \\(error)\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"I II III Error: MyError() \""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Creates an asynchronous sequence that maps the given error-throwing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closure over the asynchronous sequence’s elements.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"map","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Transformed","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":